! <solver:p610_t3>
! NAFEMS-style LE1-type distorted-CST patch test
! <BEGIN:AnalysisOptions>
! failure_criterion Elastic
! material_type Isotropic
! mesh_type T3
! solver_executable p610_t3_elastic
! <END:AnalysisOptions>
!
! Geometry (unit square with off-center interior node):
!   1 = (0, 0)         <- corner
!   2 = (1, 0)         <- corner
!   3 = (1, 1)         <- corner
!   4 = (0, 1)         <- corner
!   5 = (0.4, 0.6)     <- distorted interior node
!
! Four CST elements share node 5 (CCW ordering for outward normal = right-hand):
!   E1: 1-2-5  (bottom triangle)
!   E2: 2-3-5  (right triangle)
!   E3: 3-4-5  (top triangle)
!   E4: 4-1-5  (left triangle)
!
! Loading: uniaxial sigma = [-100, 0, 0] kPa applied via consistent edge tractions
!   on all four square boundaries. CCW edge ordering => outward normals:
!     edge 1->2 (bottom):  n = ( 0, -1), T = sigma . n = ( 0, 0)
!     edge 2->3 (right):   n = ( 1,  0), T = sigma . n = (-100, 0)
!     edge 3->4 (top):     n = ( 0,  1), T = sigma . n = ( 0, 0)
!     edge 4->1 (left):    n = (-1,  0), T = sigma . n = (100, 0)
!   Equilibrium is exact for the constant stress field; every interior CST,
!   regardless of shape distortion via node 5, must reproduce the same
!   constant stress to machine precision (the textbook patch-test pass criterion).
!
! Closed-form (plane strain, nu = 0.25, tension-positive):
!   sxx = -100, syy = 0, txy = 0, szz = nu*(sxx+syy) = -25
!
! BCs (rigid-body motion only):
!   node 1: fix x and y
!   node 2: fix y
!   node 4: fix x
! Pseudo-elastic via large cohesion / friction so plasticity never activates.
! <BEGIN:AnalysisOptions>
! failure_criterion MohrCoulomb
! material_type Isotropic
! mesh_type T3
! solver_executable p610_t3_elastoplastic
! expected_sxx_kPa -100
! expected_syy_kPa 0
! expected_txy_kPa 0
! expected_szz_kPa -25
! tolerance_kPa 1e-3
! <END:AnalysisOptions>
! Mesh size block:
! nels nn np_types
! nels = number of elements
! nn = number of nodes
! np_types = number of material/property types
4  5  1
! Material/property block:
! phi   c     psi  gamma  E        nu    K0
! One row per material/property type declared by np_types.
! Values are consumed by the selected solver in solver-specific order.
89  1.0e10  0  0  1000000  0.25  0
! Nodal coordinate block:
! One row per node in node-number order.
! Each row is: x y
0  0
1  0
1  1
0  1
0.4  0.6
! Element connectivity block:
! One row per element in element-number order.
! The node count per row identifies the element type; first row appears to be T3 triangle.
1  2  5
2  3  5
3  4  5
4  1  5
! Boundary condition block:
! First line is nr = number of restrained nodes.
! Each following row is: node_id fix_x fix_y
! 0 = fixed/restrained, 1 = free.
3
1  0  0
2  1  0
4  0  1
! Output/watch node block:
! First line is nouts = number of nodes requested for output.
! Following row(s) list the node IDs.
5
1  2  3  4  5
! Solver control block:
! tol limit incs layers
! tol = convergence tolerance
! limit = maximum iterations
! incs = load increments
! layers = solver path/layer selector
0.0001  80  3  0
! Traction loading block:
! First line is number of traction groups.
! Each group then contains:
! mode row: mode and stress/traction parameters
! edge count: number of loaded edges
! edge rows: node IDs defining each loaded boundary edge
1
0  -100  0  0
4
1  2
2  3
3  4
4  1
